16,160 dyads", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["analytic sample"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 64, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[68, 68]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 65, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[69, 69]], "note": "Model Specification subheading"}, {"id": 66, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[70, 73]], "assertion": "specified a logistic regression: logit(P(any_red_card)) ~ skin_dark_vs_light + games + position_cat + leagueCountry + yellowCards", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["logistic regression", "model specification"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 67, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[74, 74]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 68, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[75, 75]], "note": "Standard Errors and Weighting subheading"}, {"id": 69, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[76, 76]], "assertion": "used cluster-robust standard errors at the player level as the primary analysis to account for within-player correlation", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["standard errors", "clustering"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 70, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[77, 77]], "assertion": "did not apply any weighting; each dyad was weighted equally", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["weighting"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 71, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[78, 78]], "assertion": "did not include player or referee fixed effects, using covariates only", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["fixed effects"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 72, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[79, 79]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 73, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[80, 80]], "note": "Estimation Method subheading"}, {"id": 74, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[81, 81]], "assertion": "estimated the logistic regression via maximum likelihood", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["logistic regression"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 75, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[82, 82]], "assertion": "computed average marginal effects to obtain risk differences", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["average marginal effects", "risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 76, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[83, 83]], "assertion": "used alpha=0.05, two-sided tests for inference", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["inference", "alpha level"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 77, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[84, 84]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 78, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[85, 85]], "note": "Variable Transformations subheading"}, {"id": 79, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[86, 86]], "assertion": "averaged skin tone scores across the two raters", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["skin tone", "raters"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [80]}, {"id": 80, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[86, 86]], "assertion": "dichotomized the averaged skin tone score at 0.5", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["skin tone"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [79]}, {"id": 81, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[87, 87]], "assertion": "aggregated 12 detailed positions into 4 broad position categories", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["position_cat"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 82, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[88, 88]], "assertion": "used yellow cards and games as continuous variables without transformation", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["yellowCards", "games"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 83, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[89, 89]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 84, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[90, 91]], "note": "divider + blank"}, {"id": 85, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[92, 93]], "note": "Conclusion heading + blank"}, {"id": 86, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[94, 94]], "assertion": "states the conclusion as NOT SUPPORTED", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["conclusion"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 87, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[95, 95]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 88, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[96, 96]], "assertion": "the hypothesis is not definitively supported: the point estimate (0.19pp) and odds ratio (16.75% higher) point in the hypothesized direction, but p=0.053 exceeds 0.05 and the 95% CI narrowly includes zero", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["conclusion", "p-value", "confidence interval"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 89, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[97, 97]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 90, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[98, 98]], "note": "transition line introducing caveats"}, {"id": 91, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[99, 99]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 92, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[100, 100]], "assertion": "the result is extremely close to statistical significance (p=0.053), suggesting slightly different methodological choices could cross the threshold", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["p-value"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 93, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[101, 101]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 94, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[102, 102]], "assertion": "alternative specifications consistently show statistically significant effects", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["robustness checks"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 95, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[103, 103]], "assertion": "with referee clustering, RD=0.19pp, 95% CI [0.04,0.34], p=0.014", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["referee clustering", "risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 96, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[104, 104]], "assertion": "with continuous skin tone, RD=0.33pp per unit increase, 95% CI [0.05,0.60], p=0.020", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["continuous skin tone", "risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 97, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[105, 105]], "assertion": "comparing extreme skin tones only, RD=0.34pp, 95% CI [0.02,0.67], p=0.038", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["extreme skin tones", "risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 98, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[106, 106]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 99, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[107, 107]], "assertion": "the small effect (0.19pp) represents a meaningful 15% relative increase over the baseline red card rate", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["relative increase"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [100]}, {"id": 100, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[107, 107]], "assertion": "even small differences could accumulate to substantial disparities over careers given the competitive consequences of red cards", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["red cards", "careers"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": [99]}, {"id": 101, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[108, 108]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 102, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[109, 109]], "assertion": "adjusted for systematic differences between dark- and light-skinned players in position distribution and league composition", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["position", "leagueCountry"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [103]}, {"id": 103, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[109, 109]], "assertion": "residual confounding from unmeasured factors such as playing style and referee characteristics cannot be ruled out", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["confounding", "playing style", "referee characteristics"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [102]}, {"id": 104, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[110, 112]], "note": "blank/divider/blank"}, {"id": 105, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[113, 113]], "note": "Limitations heading"}, {"id": 106, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[114, 114]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 107, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[115, 115]], "note": "Measurement Issues subheading"}, {"id": 108, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[116, 116]], "note": "generic caveat that photo-based rating may not reflect real-time referee perception and introduces measurement error, no new specific action named"}, {"id": 109, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[117, 117]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 110, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[118, 118]], "assertion": "did not preserve continuous skin-tone information in the primary specification, using a dichotomized version instead which may miss non-linear relationships", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["skin tone", "dichotomization"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [111]}, {"id": 111, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[118, 118]], "assertion": "sensitivity analyses using continuous skin tone showed larger, significant effects", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["continuous skin tone"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [110]}, {"id": 112, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[119, 119]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 113, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[120, 120]], "assertion": "combined all red cards across a dyad's entire history into one outcome, obscuring temporal patterns and game-specific contexts", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["red cards", "outcome variable"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 114, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[121, 121]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 115, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[122, 122]], "note": "Selection and Confounding subheading"}, {"id": 116, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[123, 123]], "assertion": "20.5% of dyads were excluded due to missing skin tone or position data", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["exclusions"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [117]}, {"id": 117, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[123, 123]], "assertion": "players without photos may differ systematically, e.g. being less prominent players", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["missing data", "player prominence"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": [116]}, {"id": 118, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[124, 124]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 119, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[125, 129]], "note": "lists unmeasured confounders (player aggression/style, referee bias, team tactics, match importance) that cannot be fully accounted for; no specific action taken is named"}, {"id": 120, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[130, 130]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 121, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[131, 131]], "assertion": "used referee country-level implicit bias measures from Project Implicit as an indirect proxy, which risks an ecological fallacy since they don't measure individual referee attitudes", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["implicit bias measures", "referees"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 122, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[132, 132]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 123, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[133, 133]], "note": "Statistical Considerations subheading"}, {"id": 124, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[134, 134]], "assertion": "player-level clustering, used as primary, is conservative and produces larger standard errors than referee clustering", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["player clustering", "standard errors"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [125, 126]}, {"id": 125, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[134, 134]], "assertion": "two-way clustering (by player and referee) was not feasible with the available tools, so it was not used", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["two-way clustering"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [124, 126]}, {"id": 126, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[134, 134]], "assertion": "referee clustering yields a smaller p-value (p=0.014) than player clustering", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["referee clustering", "p-value"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [124, 125]}, {"id": 127, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[135, 135]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 128, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[136, 136]], "assertion": "red cards occur in only 1.25% of dyads, limiting statistical power despite the large sample size", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["red cards", "statistical power"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 129, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[137, 137]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 130, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[138, 138]], "note": "general caveat that repeated testing across robustness checks increases Type I error risk; no specific corrective action named"}, {"id": 131, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[139, 139]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 132, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[140, 140]], "note": "Assumptions subheading"}, {"id": 133, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[141, 141]], "assertion": "did not test whether the effect varies by league, position, or referee characteristics (no interaction terms)", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["interactions", "effect heterogeneity"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 134, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[142, 142]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 135, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[143, 143]], "assertion": "did not fully model complex dependencies among teammates or rivalries despite clustering adjustment", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["independence", "teammates", "rivalries"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 136, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[144, 144]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 137, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[145, 145]], "note": "general caveat that the 2012-2013, four-league data may not generalize; no specific action named"}, {"id": 138, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[146, 146]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 139, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[147, 148]], "note": "divider + blank"}, {"id": 140, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[149, 149]], "note": "Discussion of Key Assumptions heading"}, {"id": 141, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[150, 150]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 142, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[151, 151]], "note": "Assumptions Met subheading"}, {"id": 143, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[152, 152]], "assertion": "high inter-rater reliability (r=0.92) supports the validity of the skin tone measure", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["inter-rater reliability", "skin tone"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 144, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[153, 153]], "assertion": "position and league distributions differ by skin tone, justifying covariate adjustment", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["position", "leagueCountry", "skin tone"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 145, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[154, 154]], "assertion": "model fit pseudo-R² was 0.069, indicating covariates explain meaningful variation in red card likelihood", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["model fit"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 146, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[155, 155]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 147, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[156, 156]], "note": "Assumptions Not Fully Met subheading"}, {"id": 148, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[157, 157]], "assertion": "the dyadic structure violates strict independence of observations; clustering addresses but does not fully resolve this", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["independence", "clustering"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 149, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[158, 158]], "assertion": "the no-unmeasured-confounding assumption is likely violated, and the observational design precludes causal inference", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["confounding", "causal inference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 150, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[159, 159]], "assertion": "skin tone measured from photos is likely an imperfect proxy for referees' real-time perception", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["skin tone measurement"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 151, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[160, 160]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 152, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[161, 161]], "note": "Sensitivity to Assumptions subheading"}, {"id": 153, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[162, 162]], "assertion": "the primary result's borderline significance makes conclusions highly sensitive to methodological choices, with alternative approaches yielding both null and significant findings", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["sensitivity", "methodological choices"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 154, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[163, 163]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 155, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[164, 165]], "note": "divider + blank"}, {"id": 156, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[166, 166]], "note": "Methodological Transparency heading"}, {"id": 157, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[167, 167]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 158, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[168, 168]], "assertion": "provided all analysis code in final_analysis.py to support full reproducibility and documented key decisions", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["code", "reproducibility"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 159, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[169, 169]], "assertion": "chose 0.5 as the dichotomization threshold for skin tone as a median-like split", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["skin tone", "dichotomization"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 160, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[170, 170]], "assertion": "collapsed player positions into 4 broad categories", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["position_cat"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 161, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[171, 171]], "assertion": "chose player clustering as the primary approach to account for player-level heterogeneity", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["player clustering"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 162, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[172, 172]], "assertion": "used complete-case analysis (listwise deletion) for missing data", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["missing data"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 163, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[173, 173]], "assertion": "did not apply imputation, weighting, or matching", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["imputation", "weighting", "matching"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 164, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[174, 174]], "assertion": "used two-sided tests at alpha=0.05 throughout", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["inference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 165, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[175, 175]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 166, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[176, 177]], "note": "divider + blank"}, {"id": 167, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[178, 178]], "note": "Summary heading"}, {"id": 168, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[179, 179]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 169, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[180, 180]], "assertion": "overall, the analysis found inconclusive evidence: the primary result narrowly misses significance (p=0.053) while robustness checks show a consistent, small elevated red card risk for dark-skinned players that is small but potentially meaningful in competitive contexts", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["conclusion", "p-value", "robustness checks"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [170, 171]}, {"id": 170, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[180, 180]], "assertion": "causal interpretation is limited by unmeasured confounding and measurement challenges inherent in the observational data", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["confounding", "causal inference"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [169, 171]}, {"id": 171, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[180, 180]], "assertion": "recommends future research use within-referee comparisons, finer-grained situational data, and experimental designs to isolate referee decision-making from player behavior, none of which were carried out here", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["future research design"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [169, 170]}]}}